<title>FRANCE: EU MULLS SPECIAL TENDER FOR GREEK MAIZE EXPORTS.</title>
<headline>EU MULLS SPECIAL TENDER FOR GREEK MAIZE EXPORTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of the European Union's grain committee on Thursday discussed plans to open a special tender next week to allow Greece to export to non-EU countries 100,000 tonnes of maize from the open market, EU grain officials said.</p>
<p>The move, if agreed at next week's grain committee, would provide an outlet for excess maize production in Greece's northeast and so avoid sales to intervention stores, industry sources said.</p>
<p>Potential markets for Greek maize include Bulgaria, Turkey and possibly Malta, they said. -- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
